# Store every file byte-for-byte and never apply end-of-line conversion.
#
# The patch series has to apply cleanly, and .gitignore.baseline in particular ends
# with a single CR that is load-bearing. Git's default eol handling on Windows, and
# any ambient core.autocrlf=true, would rewrite line endings on checkout and change
# the blob hashes - which breaks `git am` and invalidates the audited tree hash
# f86ca17e735fbf24d8762a94334c1e7218718549 the build verifies against.
#
# Marking everything as non-text disables CRLF normalisation in both directions.
# It costs nothing here: there is no line-ending workflow to preserve in a repo of
# patches and scripts.
* -text
